        "min_height": 520,
        "background": "cream",
        "heading": "Colour",
        "text": "<p>Diamonds come in a variety of colours, ranging from colourless, clear diamonds to those that have a yellow or brown tint. The less colour, the higher the grade and the more desirable & valuable they are.</p><p>A diamonds colour is determined on a scale from 'D' (colourless) to 'Z' (yellow/ brown). Most diamonds used in jewellery are nearly colourless with pale tints of yellow or brown.</p>"
